%chk=probe_ni_porphine_triplet.chk
%mem=16GB
%nprocshared=8
#P ROHF/6-31G NoSymm Int=NoBasisTransform SCF=(Conver=10,MaxCycle=256)
# Output=(MatrixElement,MO2ElectronIntegrals) Tran=(Full,Force) Window=(84,104)

probe_ni_porphine_triplet: the same molecule, geometry and window as the singlet, as an ROHF triplet. THE POINT: this is the legacy comparison the project was built around. The two shipped dumps in legacy/ put the Fe-porphyrin ROHF triplet 0.673 Ha BELOW the RHF singlet, which is impossible, and 186 of their 210 one-electron off-diagonals are exactly zero -- the fingerprint of the diagonal-Fock assumption. Run this and the singlet, dump both, and the triplet reference must come out ABOVE the singlet. That is the fix, measured on a real system rather than on CH2. Expect NELEC=22, MS2=2, active occupied 12 alpha and 10 beta. If ROHF struggles to converge, add Guess=Read after running the singlet, since the .chk is right there.

